WEBVTT

00:06:29.134 --> 00:06:32.165
So his greeting was not particularly
warm, but they did say,

00:06:32.189 --> 00:06:35.832
well, OK -- let's hear
your questions on your survey.

00:06:36.260 --> 00:06:37.465
So -- I kid you not --

00:06:37.489 --> 00:06:41.276
the first question on the survey
that he was sent to ask was:

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:44.006
"How do you feel about being
poor and Black in America?"

00:06:44.030 --> 00:06:47.161
(Laughter)

00:06:47.185 --> 00:06:48.876
Makes you wonder about academics.

00:06:48.900 --> 00:06:50.804
(Laughter)

00:06:50.828 --> 00:06:52.709
So the choice of answers were:

00:06:52.733 --> 00:06:56.380
[A) Very Good B) Good C) Bad D) Very Bad]

00:06:56.404 --> 00:06:58.405
(Laughter)

00:06:58.429 --> 00:07:01.934
What Sudhir found out is, in fact,
that the real answer was the following: